{"tool": "finish", "summary": "Added a nullable `entries.word_count` column (new migration, no backfill: existing entries stay null until saved again). The storage layer computes the count on every entry write (createEntry, updateEntry, UpdateEntryTitleAndContent) as whitespace-separated words of the content after sanitizer.StripTags, and sets it on the entry. The entry query builder reads it back, and `model.Entry` / `client.Entry` expose it as `word_count` (`*int`, null where unknown). Build and existing unit and integration tests pass; no tests were added for the new behaviour. Note: because tags are simply removed, text in adjacent block elements with no whitespace between them (e.g. `<p>one</p><p>two</p>`) counts as one word.", "t": 1794463634.317}
